# What the sdist carries beyond the package itself.
#
# setuptools' own default sweeps up files matching test*.py and nothing else, so
# the 0.4.0 sdist shipped tests/test_*.py without tests/conftest.py, the fixture
# data they read, or tests/synthetic.py -- `pytest` in an unpacked sdist failed
# at collection. That is worth more than tidiness: conda-forge builds from the
# sdist and runs the test suite, and so does anyone packaging this downstream.
include LICENSE
include CHANGELOG.md
include README.md
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include tests/data *
